In this paper, we propose an enhanced method that combines an IMU based step counter and live video feed to improve the previously introduced natural marker based augmented reality framework for indoor navigation. In addition to AR based natural marker detection and tracking, IMU data is used to estimate the position and orientation of the mobile device in cases where sole vision based concepts fail. Based on the IMU acceleration data, a step counter is implemented. In conjunction with the IMU magnetic compass and an estimated pre-defined step length, the step counter is able to extrapolate the device’s motion. It is expected to improve pose estimation performance, in particular, in cases where either no natural marker is available in the live camera view or where identical markers are available several times.

