3.1. IMU based step counter

As depicted in Fig. 5 a below, the procedure of implementing an IMU based step counter can be divided into four stages: Collect acceleration data, transform to global coordinates, streamline data using filters, and detect and count steps [40] . This part of the enhanced method is neither new nor a contribution of this paper. There are several different methods on how to use IMU data to estimate continuous user movement (e.g. [40] ). However, for completeness reasons and in order to better understand the integration of IMU data into the AR framework and its re-calibration, the procedure of detecting footsteps is described below.

